# Eq. (119) defect→chart spine and the terminal physical-carrier round (Lean lane)

This round turned the latest source-side and terminal-side findings into
machine-checked Lean in `RequestProject/YangMills/`.  Everything below compiles
in the full `lake build RequestProject`, contains no `sorry`, no `axiom` and no
`@[implemented_by]`, and every headline theorem is audited with `#print axioms`
(only `propext`, `Classical.choice`, `Quot.sound`).

## 1. Source side: from the stored-bond budget to the principal logarithm

`SU2QuaternionOperatorNorm.lean`, `RelativeHolonomyDefect.lean`,
`SU2PrincipalChart.lean`, `Eq119RelativeLogSpine.lean`, `Eq119SpineChecks.lean`.

* The quaternion-to-matrix representation `su2 : Quaternion ℝ → Matrix (Fin 2) (Fin 2) ℂ`
  is a multiplicative, star-preserving map, and its **L² operator norm equals the
  quaternion norm** (`su2_norm`).  This closes the representation seam that the
  source-side report flagged as row B: `‖U − I‖_op ≤ ‖quaternion coordinates‖₁`
  is now a theorem (`su2_defect_le_l1`), not a receipt.
* Signed links are eliminated: a negative traversal is the group inverse of the
  stored positive bond, and `l1defect_star` shows the defect functional is
  inversion invariant.  So the only quantitative input is the **stored positive
  bond budget** `δ(U_b) ≤ 1/2048`.
* `holonomy_relative` proves the same-object identity
  `Hol(Γ ‖ c⁻¹) = Hol(Γ) · Hol(c)⁻¹`, and `relative_holonomy_defect_le`
  telescopes the 74 oriented links of the canonical `L = 13`, radius‑6 contour
  word to `74/2048 = 37/1024`, hence `< 1/24`
  (`relative_holonomy_defect_lt_inv24`).
* `principal_chart_of_defect_le_inv24` proves the chart admission
  `δ(U) ≤ 1/24 ⟹ U ∈ PrincipalImage` for the explicit quaternion logarithm
  `qlog`, with `exp (qlog U) = U` and `‖qlog U‖ < π/2`.
* `relative_log_spine` composes these: the stored-bond budget alone yields
  `Y_x = qlog (U(Γ_{c,x}) U(c)⁻¹)` with `exp (i Y_x) = U(Γ_{c,x})U(c)⁻¹` and the
  quantitative bound `‖Y‖ ≤ arccos(1 − 37/1024)`.
* `Eq119SpineChecks.lean` exhibits an explicit rational unit quaternion and a
  74-link word satisfying the hypotheses, so the spine is **not vacuous**.

The physical hypothesis that remains displayed (and is *not* claimed proved) is
that the Eq. (119) bond field is the selected Bałaban background with the
`1/2048` per-bond budget.

## 2. Terminal side: physical carrier, quotient, generator, gap

`PhysicalNullQuotient.lean`, `GeneratorUniquenessCore.lean`,
`PhysicalTimeEvolutionGenerator.lean`, `GaugeInvariantL2Carrier.lean`,
`GaugeInvariantCarrierWitness.lean`, `MassGapFormTransport.lean`.

* **Separation is a theorem.**  For a semi-inner product, equality of all weak
  pairings *is* the physical null relation (`nullRel_iff_forall_inner_eq`), so
  the "null-class separating pairing" item needs no receipt.  Consequently two
  operators with equal weak pairings have equal descended operators
  (`descend_congr_of_forall_inner_eq`).
* **Symmetry already implies null preservation**
  (`preservesNull_of_isSymmetricOp`): the integration-by-parts identity and the
  "H preserves the null ideal" requirement are the *same* payment, not two.
* **Generator uniqueness needs no Stone theorem.**  `GeneratorUniquenessCore`
  proves that two — possibly unbounded — candidate Hamiltonians differentiating
  the same orbit map on a common core agree there
  (`generator_unique_of_evolution_eq`), and are equal as operators if bounded on
  a dense core (`generator_clm_unique`).  This is the uniqueness content of
  `U_t^{YM} = U_t^{OS} ⟹ H_YM = H_Stone`, obtained from uniqueness of
  derivatives alone.
* **The carrier is literal.**  `GaugeInvariantL2Carrier` builds the physical
  Hilbert space as the gauge-invariant subspace of `L²(μ)` for one arbitrary
  measure `μ` with a measure-preserving gauge action: invariance is a closed
  submodule, hence complete; the pairing is definite; gauge-commuting operators
  restrict and stay symmetric.  No fresh counting measure, no generic GNS state,
  no extra quotient framework.
* **Non-vacuity.**  `GaugeInvariantCarrierWitness` instantiates the carrier on
  the finite group `ZMod 2` with its Haar (counting) measure and the nontrivial
  left-translation gauge action, and exhibits a nonzero invariant wavefunction.
* **Uniform gaps survive limits.**  `MassGapFormTransport` proves that a
  uniform form gap `Δ` above a fixed vacuum passes to a *strong* limit of
  Hamiltonians (`hasFormGap_of_tendsto`), also with converging gap constants.
  This is the "no spectral pollution from below" step at the level at which the
  gap is consumed, and it assumes no norm/resolvent convergence or compactness.

## 3. What is still open

Nothing here claims the Clay theorem, nor any physical closure.  The
still-unpaid physical inputs are, unchanged in substance:

1. the Eq. (119) bond field is the selected physical Bałaban background with the
   `1/2048` stored-bond budget;
2. the literal Yang–Mills Hamiltonian is the selected action variation on the
   gauge-invariant carrier, with a common invariant dense core;
3. the physical time evolution `U_t^{YM}` and the OS-reconstructed evolution are
   the same one-parameter family on that carrier;
4. the finite-to-continuum construction producing a strongly convergent family
   of Hamiltonians with a uniform gap, and the OS/Wightman-axiom package on the
   continuum object.

Items 1–4 are hypotheses of the corresponding Lean statements, displayed rather
than discharged.  What this round removed from the list is the machinery around
them: representation identification, defect telescoping, chart admission,
separation, null preservation, generator uniqueness, carrier completeness and
gap stability are now theorems.
